# Inert until collections-as-call-arguments lands (sub-bindings are numeric-only) — see Future.md. The fold itself is proven equivalent to the C++ reducer (tests.cpp).
# count_of(xs) — element count of a seq collection, as a foldl that increments
# the accumulator by 1 per element. SPEC definition; coexists with the C++
# `count` fast-path and is proven equivalent. Empty collection -> 0.
@include "count_op.fw"
[count_of(xs) -> result]
result = foldl(xs, count_op, 0)
